<title>BELGIUM: GENERALE BANK GROUP NET UP 10.4 PCT.</title>
<headline>GENERALE BANK GROUP NET UP 10.4 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full-year 1996</p>
<p>(billions of Belgian francs, unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net (excludes minorities)	  15.10 vs     13.67</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)			  395 vs	 385</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total		     5,544    vs  4,739   </p>
<p>Note - Generale Bank said in a statement that its 1996</p>
<p>consolidated accounts for the first time include the earnings of</p>
<p>Dutch unit Generale Bank Nederland and of French unit Fimagest.</p>
<p>Its GMIC stake was no longer consolidated. If there had been no</p>
<p>changes to the consolidation perimeter, group net profit would</p>
<p>have risen 8.2 percent instead of 10.4 percent.</p>
<p>    Net interest income			  82.89 vs     71.73</p>
<p>    Non-interest income			  49.10 vs     41.61</p>
<p>	of which commercial activities	 26.17 vs     20.05</p>
<p>	of which capital gains		   13.05 vs     10.35</p>
<p>    Gross income				  131.99 vs    113.35</p>
<p>    General expenses			    -78.99 vs    -68.16</p>
<p>	of which staff costs		    -54.88 vs    -47.70</p>
<p>    Gross profit				   53.02 vs     45.18</p>
<p>    Depreciation,write-downs,provisions   -22.03 vs     20.16</p>
<p>    Extraordinary loss			   -2.85 vs     -0.77</p>
<p>    Tax					     -10.47 vs     -8.06</p>
<p>    Own funds					 129 vs    107    </p>
<p>    Customer deposits, bank savings cert. 2,908 vs   2,705</p>
<p>    Private sector credits		    2,060 vs   1,763</p>
<p>    Public sector credits		     1,171 vs   1,025</p>
<p>    Risk asset ratio (in percentage)	10.66 vs   10.54</p>
<p>    Return on equity  (in pct)		12.80 vs   13.11 *</p>
<p>    Net profit per share (in francs)	 914  vs   914 *</p>
<p>NOTE - * Taking into account the data on which the capital</p>
<p>increase occured (October 1996) rather than the period for which</p>
<p>holders of new shares were entitled to a dividend (twelve</p>
<p>months), net earnings per share were 982 francs.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
